1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,060
You know your star sign. Maybe you are a
Leo. Maybe a Scorpio. Maybe a Capricorn.

2
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:10,030
And you have probably read your horoscope
at least once and thought: "Okay.

3
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:11,930
That actually sounds like me."

4
00:00:12,615 --> 00:00:15,465
But here is a strange question. Why?

5
00:00:15,895 --> 00:00:18,975
Why should the position of
Mars, Venus or Jupiter on the

6
00:00:19,055 --> 00:00:21,725
day you were born have anything
to do with who you are?

7
00:00:22,377 --> 00:00:25,437
And if the stars really do
decide what you are like, why

8
00:00:25,517 --> 00:00:28,847
can't astrologers even agree
on which sign you belong to?

9
00:00:29,535 --> 00:00:32,425
Because there is a rather large
problem hiding in the sky.

10
00:00:33,255 --> 00:00:34,845
It is called Ophiuchus.

11
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:41,885
The zodiac supposedly has twelve signs.
Aries. Taurus. Gemini. Cancer. Leo. Virgo.

12
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:47,605
Libra. Scorpio. Sagittarius. Capricorn.
Aquarius. Pisces. Nice and tidy.

13
00:00:47,685 --> 00:00:51,035
Twelve signs. Twelve
months. Everything fits.

14
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:55,415
Except the Sun does not actually
pass through twelve constellations.

15
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,160
It passes through thirteen.

16
00:00:58,630 --> 00:01:01,740
The thirteenth is Ophiuchus.
The Serpent Bearer.

17
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:04,890
And yes, the Sun really
does move across it every

18
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:07,740
year, for nearly three weeks,
from the end of November.

19
00:01:08,595 --> 00:01:12,795
So if your personality is decided by
the constellation behind the Sun on the

20
00:01:12,875 --> 00:01:17,745
day you were born, what happens if you
were born while the Sun was in Ophiuchus?

21
00:01:18,462 --> 00:01:20,812
Are you a Scorpio? A Sagittarius?

22
00:01:20,922 --> 00:01:22,812
Or the forbidden thirteenth sign?

23
00:01:23,582 --> 00:01:27,212
Western astrology has an answer,
and it is a perfectly good one.

24
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:31,770
Its twelve signs were never based on
the boundaries of the constellations.

25
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:35,500
There is no thirteenth sign
to add, because the signs

26
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:38,550
of astrology are not the
constellations in the sky.

27
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:43,540
Because the real
constellations do not sit in

28
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:46,510
twelve equal slices of
thirty degrees each.

29
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:51,770
They are different sizes, and the Sun
spends different amounts of time in them.

30
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,770
So the real sky looks something like this.

31
00:01:55,499 --> 00:01:57,929
And the astrological
zodiac looks like this.

32
00:01:58,759 --> 00:02:00,549
The second one is wonderfully neat.

33
00:02:01,239 --> 00:02:03,449
The first one is what the sky really does.

34
00:02:05,779 --> 00:02:09,419
So what is a sign, if it is
not a star? It is an angle.

35
00:02:09,499 --> 00:02:12,719
Thirty degrees of a
circle that starts where

36
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,559
the Sun stands on the first day of spring.

37
00:02:14,639 --> 00:02:18,669
Pinned to our seasons,
not to anything out there.

38
00:02:19,321 --> 00:02:23,011
And that matters, because the
Earth is wobbling. Very slowly.

39
00:02:24,101 --> 00:02:27,281
Its axis of rotation precesses,
like a spinning top, and

40
00:02:27,361 --> 00:02:30,471
one full wobble takes roughly
twenty-six thousand years.

41
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,940
So the first day of spring creeps
along the sky, about one degree

42
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:39,710
every seventy-two years, away from
the stars it once lined up with.

43
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,550
Western astrology does not mind.

44
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,770
Its signs follow the seasons,
and the seasons have not moved.

45
00:02:47,602 --> 00:02:51,332
But the astrology practised across
India made the opposite choice.

46
00:02:52,122 --> 00:02:55,512
It kept its signs tied to the stars,
and it corrects for the drift.

47
00:02:56,425 --> 00:02:58,695
That correction has a name and a number.

48
00:02:59,405 --> 00:03:01,375
Today it is about twenty-four degrees.

49
00:03:01,665 --> 00:03:03,975
Which is most of a whole sign.

50
00:03:04,739 --> 00:03:06,139
So take one person.

51
00:03:06,219 --> 00:03:09,309
One birth, one sky, one set of planets.

52
00:03:09,659 --> 00:03:12,309
Western astrology calls them a Leo.

53
00:03:13,179 --> 00:03:15,369
Indian astrology calls them a Cancer.

54
00:03:16,297 --> 00:03:18,757
Work out how often that
happens and it comes

55
00:03:18,837 --> 00:03:21,287
to roughly four people out of every five.

56
00:03:21,997 --> 00:03:26,647
Four in five would get a different sign
depending on which astrologer they asked.

57
00:03:27,488 --> 00:03:30,638
Which gives the question we
started with a much sharper edge.

58
00:03:31,548 --> 00:03:35,768
If two systems cannot even agree on
which thirty-degree slice is yours, the

59
00:03:35,848 --> 00:03:40,138
real question is why thirty degrees of
anything should describe a person at all.

60
00:03:43,138 --> 00:03:44,788
Fine, says astrology.

61
00:03:45,638 --> 00:03:47,208
The signs are only the frame.

62
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:51,788
The important thing is the exact
position of the planets. All right.

63
00:03:51,938 --> 00:03:53,608
Let us calculate a horoscope.

64
00:03:54,699 --> 00:03:57,619
Give an astrologer your date
of birth, your exact time of

65
00:03:57,699 --> 00:04:01,129
birth, and the place, and they
can calculate your birth chart.

66
00:04:02,001 --> 00:04:05,791
Where the Sun, the Moon and the planets
stood is worked out astronomically.

67
00:04:06,581 --> 00:04:08,051
That is the easy part.

68
00:04:08,904 --> 00:04:11,184
A computer can tell you
where every planet was

69
00:04:11,264 --> 00:04:14,234
that morning, to a fraction
of a second of arc.

70
00:04:14,995 --> 00:04:16,745
But then comes the interesting bit.

71
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:22,725
The astrologer interprets them. Mars
means one thing. Venus means another.

72
00:04:23,735 --> 00:04:25,245
Saturn means something else.

73
00:04:26,041 --> 00:04:29,751
Then you add houses. And
aspects. And the ascendant.

74
00:04:30,321 --> 00:04:34,191
And suddenly a list of coordinates
has become a personality profile.

75
00:04:35,141 --> 00:04:38,621
The planets are real. The
calculations are real.

76
00:04:38,701 --> 00:04:40,791
The interpretation is something else.

77
00:04:41,661 --> 00:04:45,091
It is a system of symbolic
meanings. And here is the question.

78
00:04:46,001 --> 00:04:48,651
Why should those meanings
match a human personality?

79
00:04:49,686 --> 00:04:52,326
What connects the position
of Saturn, more than

80
00:04:52,406 --> 00:04:54,856
a billion kilometres away,
with your temperament?

81
00:04:55,841 --> 00:04:57,431
There is no known mechanism.

82
00:04:58,161 --> 00:04:59,791
And gravity does not help.

83
00:05:00,241 --> 00:05:02,301
Jupiter does pull on a newborn, of course.

84
00:05:02,381 --> 00:05:04,211
But gravity is just gravity.

85
00:05:05,199 --> 00:05:07,399
It carries no message
saying this child will

86
00:05:07,479 --> 00:05:10,249
be optimistic and that
one will be ambitious.

87
00:05:11,247 --> 00:05:15,247
And even if it somehow did, it still
would not explain why astrologers

88
00:05:15,327 --> 00:05:18,557
give each planet a completely
different psychological meaning.

89
00:05:21,377 --> 00:05:23,217
That is a rather serious problem for a

90
00:05:23,297 --> 00:05:25,787
system that claims to
tell you who you are.

91
00:05:26,437 --> 00:05:29,027
And there is another
wonderfully arbitrary part.

92
00:05:29,977 --> 00:05:31,787
Why the exact moment of birth?

93
00:05:32,635 --> 00:05:34,045
Imagine two babies.

94
00:05:34,975 --> 00:05:39,085
One is born a minute before midnight. The
other a minute after. Two minutes apart.

95
00:05:39,965 --> 00:05:44,075
And suddenly the planets have moved just
enough to give them different horoscopes.

96
00:05:44,845 --> 00:05:46,515
But what about the moment of conception?

97
00:05:47,505 --> 00:05:49,075
What about the first heartbeat?

98
00:05:50,049 --> 00:05:52,709
Or the moment the doctor
actually wrote the time down?

99
00:05:52,789 --> 00:05:55,139
Which one is cosmically important?

100
00:05:56,149 --> 00:06:00,139
Nature does not appear to contain a
magical switch labelled: "Personality.

101
00:06:00,509 --> 00:06:01,709
Calculate now."

102
00:06:04,149 --> 00:06:07,779
And yet astrology treats that one
moment as enormously significant.

103
00:06:08,469 --> 00:06:10,199
Fine, you might say.

104
00:06:10,449 --> 00:06:15,079
But my horoscope is always accurate.
All right. Let us try something.

105
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,163
Here is a horoscope.

106
00:06:18,053 --> 00:06:21,603
You are generally a thoughtful person,
but you sometimes doubt yourself.

107
00:06:22,473 --> 00:06:25,883
You value close relationships,
although you also need time alone.

108
00:06:26,706 --> 00:06:29,606
You can be very determined
when something matters to you.

109
00:06:29,686 --> 00:06:33,116
And at times you are rather
too critical of yourself.

110
00:06:33,993 --> 00:06:39,073
How accurate is that? Pretty good? Maybe
surprisingly good? Here is the problem.

111
00:06:39,153 --> 00:06:40,873
That description was not written for you.

112
00:06:40,953 --> 00:06:42,823
It could have been
written for almost anyone.

113
00:06:43,732 --> 00:06:45,482
And that is not an accident.

114
00:06:46,192 --> 00:06:47,822
It is called the Barnum effect.

115
00:06:48,572 --> 00:06:50,652
Or the Forer effect,
after the psychologist

116
00:06:50,732 --> 00:06:52,302
who tested it in nineteen forty-eight.

117
00:06:54,136 --> 00:06:56,296
He handed thirty-nine
students what he told

118
00:06:56,376 --> 00:06:59,026
them were personal personality profiles.

119
00:06:59,916 --> 00:07:03,566
He had assembled the text out
of a newsstand astrology book.

120
00:07:04,282 --> 00:07:06,792
Every student got exactly the same one.

121
00:07:07,542 --> 00:07:11,932
Then he asked them to rate it, from zero
to five, for how well it described them.

122
00:07:12,702 --> 00:07:13,902
The average was four point two six.

123
00:07:15,539 --> 00:07:17,369
Only then did he tell them the truth.

124
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:23,179
And many of them still said: "But that
is me." So are horoscopes just random?

125
00:07:23,259 --> 00:07:26,589
Not exactly. This is
where we have to be fair.

126
00:07:29,129 --> 00:07:31,489
A professional astrologer
is not sitting there

127
00:07:31,569 --> 00:07:34,439
pressing a button marked
"random horoscope".

128
00:07:35,177 --> 00:07:37,307
The positions really are calculated.

129
00:07:38,277 --> 00:07:41,567
The chart really is built according
to an elaborate set of rules.

130
00:07:42,443 --> 00:07:44,553
But those rules rest on one assumption.

131
00:07:45,503 --> 00:07:48,093
That the positions mean
something about a person.

132
00:07:48,543 --> 00:07:51,313
And that is the assumption
that needs evidence.

133
00:07:52,271 --> 00:07:56,741
Because you could replace the whole system
with a text generator. Pick a tendency.

134
00:07:57,111 --> 00:08:02,681
Add some ambiguity. Mention relationships,
or a career, or personal growth.

135
00:08:03,548 --> 00:08:05,338
And you get something like this.

136
00:08:06,028 --> 00:08:09,378
"The coming weeks may bring some
uncertainty in your relationships,

137
00:08:09,968 --> 00:08:13,138
but they could also open an
opportunity for personal growth."

138
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:17,600
Did Mars cause that sentence?
No. I just wrote it.

139
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:20,600
And yet, does it sound like
it could be your horoscope?

140
00:08:21,070 --> 00:08:23,880
This is where the argument
stops being philosophical.

141
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:26,600
Because we can actually test it.

142
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:32,100
If astrology works, then an
astrologer should be able to

143
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:35,290
match a birth chart to a
person better than chance can.

144
00:08:36,065 --> 00:08:41,015
In nineteen eighty-five, a double-blind
test of astrology was published in Nature.

145
00:08:42,145 --> 00:08:44,445
Astrologers helped
design it, and they said

146
00:08:44,525 --> 00:08:46,655
in advance what would count as success.

147
00:08:47,585 --> 00:08:49,595
Their own figure was one in two.

148
00:08:50,373 --> 00:08:53,173
Each of them was handed a birth
chart and three personality

149
00:08:53,253 --> 00:08:57,123
profiles, and asked which of the
three belonged to that chart.

150
00:08:58,021 --> 00:09:00,111
Guessing alone would get one in three.

151
00:09:00,921 --> 00:09:03,161
The original analysis found
nothing better than chance.

152
00:09:03,241 --> 00:09:05,951
Forty right out of a hundred and sixteen.

153
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:09,889
But the statistics were later disputed.

154
00:09:10,859 --> 00:09:13,339
Add up the answers a different
way and a faint signal

155
00:09:13,419 --> 00:09:16,309
appears, right on the
edge of meaning anything.

156
00:09:17,206 --> 00:09:21,916
Which is why one experiment is never
the last word. Including this one.

157
00:09:22,746 --> 00:09:25,706
So the question is not what
a single study found, but

158
00:09:25,786 --> 00:09:28,896
whether astrologers beat chance
when you keep testing them.

159
00:09:29,549 --> 00:09:31,699
More than forty such tests exist.

160
00:09:32,809 --> 00:09:35,849
Nearly seven hundred astrologers,
over a thousand birth charts.

161
00:09:35,929 --> 00:09:40,439
Pooled together, the effect is
indistinguishable from nothing.

162
00:09:41,169 --> 00:09:44,359
And there is a second measurement
that needs nobody to be right.

163
00:09:44,869 --> 00:09:48,579
Give one chart to two astrologers
and ask them what it says.

164
00:09:49,374 --> 00:09:52,474
Across twenty-five studies,
their agreement comes out at

165
00:09:52,554 --> 00:09:55,864
about one tenth, on a scale
where one would be perfect.

166
00:09:56,766 --> 00:09:58,996
For a test you would
actually use on a person,

167
00:09:59,226 --> 00:10:01,616
psychologists want eight tenths or better.

168
00:10:02,606 --> 00:10:07,096
Before you can ask whether astrology is
true, it has to say the same thing twice.

169
00:10:08,043 --> 00:10:09,833
And that is the key distinction.

170
00:10:10,883 --> 00:10:12,963
It does not matter
whether an astrologer can

171
00:10:13,043 --> 00:10:15,613
produce an explanation
that sounds convincing.

172
00:10:16,546 --> 00:10:20,096
What matters is whether it predicts
something before we know the answer.

173
00:10:20,966 --> 00:10:23,856
That is how you tell a real
effect from a good story.

174
00:10:26,696 --> 00:10:29,226
And here is where this
gets much more interesting.

175
00:10:29,756 --> 00:10:33,106
Because people who believe
in astrology are not stupid.

176
00:10:33,941 --> 00:10:38,991
Astrology appeals to something our brains
are extremely good at. Finding patterns.

177
00:10:39,241 --> 00:10:40,441
Finding meaning.

178
00:10:41,013 --> 00:10:43,643
Remembering the hits.
Forgetting the misses.

179
00:10:43,733 --> 00:10:47,643
And building a coherent story
out of incomplete information.

180
00:10:48,684 --> 00:10:51,724
If your horoscope says you may
meet a difficult situation this

181
00:10:51,804 --> 00:10:56,214
week, and something annoying happens
on Thursday, you remember it.

182
00:10:56,908 --> 00:10:58,838
If nothing happens, you do not.

183
00:10:59,228 --> 00:11:01,608
And if it says you may
go through a period of

184
00:11:01,688 --> 00:11:04,338
emotional uncertainty,
that cannot be wrong.

185
00:11:04,508 --> 00:11:06,898
You can always find something.

186
00:11:09,348 --> 00:11:11,218
So let us go back to the beginning.

187
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:13,668
You were told that your personality was

188
00:11:13,748 --> 00:11:16,138
written in the sky on
the day you were born.

189
00:11:16,913 --> 00:11:19,143
But the signs are not the constellations.

190
00:11:19,893 --> 00:11:22,353
There are thirteen of
those on the Sun's path,

191
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:25,343
not twelve, and they are
not equal pieces of sky.

192
00:11:26,153 --> 00:11:30,943
Two whole schools of astrology disagree
by nearly a sign about which one is yours.

193
00:11:31,818 --> 00:11:35,738
No known force carries a personality
from Saturn to a delivery room.

194
00:11:35,818 --> 00:11:40,668
And a description written for everybody
can feel like it was written for you.

195
00:11:41,303 --> 00:11:45,333
So does that prove that every
astrologer is a fraud? No.

196
00:11:45,443 --> 00:11:47,193
It proves something much simpler.

197
00:11:47,943 --> 00:11:49,873
The claims of astrology need evidence.

198
00:11:50,915 --> 00:11:53,615
And when they are tested
carefully, astrology does

199
00:11:53,695 --> 00:11:56,545
not behave like something
that can predict a person.

200
00:11:59,465 --> 00:12:02,995
And perhaps that is the most
fascinating thing about astrology.

201
00:12:03,945 --> 00:12:07,535
Not that Mars controls your
personality. It does not.

202
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:12,363
Not that Saturn knows what will
happen to your career. It does not.

203
00:12:13,133 --> 00:12:15,493
The fascinating part is
that your brain can look at

204
00:12:15,573 --> 00:12:19,023
a handful of vague sentences
and say: "That is me."

205
00:12:19,757 --> 00:12:21,407
We are pattern-recognition machines.

206
00:12:22,157 --> 00:12:23,587
We see faces in clouds.

207
00:12:24,477 --> 00:12:26,387
We see shapes in random noise.

208
00:12:26,497 --> 00:12:28,147
We connect unrelated events.

209
00:12:29,031 --> 00:12:33,261
And sometimes we see meaning in
the planets. The stars are real.

210
00:12:33,891 --> 00:12:36,561
The planets are real.
The mathematics is real.

211
00:12:37,551 --> 00:12:40,581
The question is whether the story
we have built around them is.

212
00:12:41,357 --> 00:12:43,297
So the next time your
horoscope tells you that

213
00:12:43,377 --> 00:12:46,067
something important is
about to happen, remember.

214
00:12:46,537 --> 00:12:51,307
The universe probably is not sending
you a message. Your brain is.
